{"type": "message", "id": "c1fe428e", "parentId": "3690578f", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T06:26:09.672Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool-7588b3292bfd4aebb99e40e6b60e5a6f", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:nationsreportcard.gov grade 8 mathematics 2022 state scores Kansas Arizona South Carolina Kentucky\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 830,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8681045fa9aab950\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8681045fa9aab950\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2de83bd6f5879cd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e2de83bd6f5879cd\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c06316b86f23dc54\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c06316b86f23dc54\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63f725b8c7a0f34e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, average mathematics scores at eighth grade declined in all four census-defined regions of the country—Northeast, Midwest, South, and West. Scores were <strong>lower by 9, 8, 8, and 6 points, respectively, compared to 2019.</strong> Looking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63f725b8c7a0f34e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a2d870f1a942f9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a2d870f1a942f9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb0376928c8ad50d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, <strong>female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb0376928c8ad50d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51139518a7245067\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51139518a7245067\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cc96d51e85a6c2f3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cc96d51e85a6c2f3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d88b0e34893558f0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d88b0e34893558f0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee2e4689c3d711c1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ee2e4689c3d711c1\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:nationsreportcard.gov grade 8 mathematics 2022 state scores Kansas Arizona South Carolina Kentucky", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 830, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8681045fa9aab950\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8681045fa9aab950\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e2de83bd6f5879cd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe table below shows the number of states/jurisdictions with score increases or decreases in 2022 and how many states/jurisdictions scored higher, lower, or not significantly different than the nation (public) in NAEP mathematics.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e2de83bd6f5879cd\">>>", "siteName": "www.nationsreportcard.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c06316b86f23dc54\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c06316b86f23dc54\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERN